From af3629585c6a1b77292349a58eb5b9291d5dbcd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:06:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] Check imported segment geometry on stream reads (#1915)

A provider answering a segment's id with another file's article at the same
offset was played (or padded to size) because stream reads only checked the
=ypart offset. Segments now carry a BodyExpectation from the imported layout:
trusted sizes give the offset and decoded length, and for a whole NZB file the
=ybegin size. Stream fetches, cache flights and hedges pass it to the new
Client::body_expecting; a mismatch fails over like a corrupt copy and is never
padded. The =ybegin size and part are checked before any byte reaches
progress, so a streamed head never serves another file's prefix.
